	"nodes":[
		{"id":"eb2b9ff8a175d224","type":"text","text":"# Discord API","x":-700,"y":-440,"width":480,"height":80},
		{"id":"1792a8f9104febec","type":"text","text":"# Interaction","x":-1010,"y":-220,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"9454b9105aa496e0","type":"text","text":"# Commad\nEg: a Ping command","x":-1010,"y":20,"width":290,"height":140},
		{"id":"4910bf85006fe8c5","type":"text","text":"# Page object\nPage is a blue print that tells `app` what it looks like and what it does. A Page is made up by a `DOM` architecture that at render time resolves closures and renders to Discord Components v2.\nAt startup time the Page obj will bind it's self to the `app` and provide an unique id for it and all of its children.\nAll of the closures for the interactable elements of this, such as buttons or dropdowns, will be internally linked to in the `app` ","x":-160,"y":-170,"width":720,"height":380},
		{"id":"4a6520b34744e0ea","type":"text","text":"#","x":-1460,"y":320,"width":740,"height":160},
		{"id":"8d7c517ef4f7a13e","type":"text","text":"# Button","x":-1340,"y":20,"width":210,"height":80},
		{"id":"abe0181d977f7c7b","type":"text","text":"# App\n```rust\npub struct App {\n\tdb: DB\n\tPages: HachMap<String, Box<dyn PageHandler>>\n}\n```\nApp is the monolithic Object that controls data flow from the Discord API to the Page callbacks. It works like this:\nThe code that the buttons and other interactions us in defined in the page\nA Page is registered in app.\nWhen the page is rendered the path to the button's callbacks are stored in the db with the serialized generic that page was defined to support eg:\n```rust\nlet page = Page::<UserLevelInfo>::new(\"UsersLevel\")\n\t.add_action_row([\n\t\tButton::new(\"See Level\", \"ButtonID\", ButtonStyle::Secondary, |app, data: UserLevelInfo| move async {\n\t\t\ttodo!();\n\t\t})\n\t]);\n```\nthe path to the callback would be something like: `UsersLevel.ButtonID` both that and the serialized version of `UserLevelInfo` are hashed together. `UserLevelInfo` is got at render time because the method for render is: `page.render(app, user_level: UsersLevel)` and user level would look like:\n```rust\nstruct UserLevelInfo {\n\tuser_id: String\n}\n```\nso at render time app will put into the DB something like this:\n```\nHASH: dbyuwg8732gvuycgsd7hgft8y34...\nPATH: UsersLevel.ButtonID\nDATA: {\"user_id\":\"715043871503024218\"}\n```\nand the page will render the custom id for the button to be the hash that is in the DB,\nThen the massage is sent,\nWhen the user clicks the button the app takes a look at the custom_id and looks it up in the DB,\nWhen it finds it in the db the App uses the Path to find the Page obj and because the page obj serialize the data it is passed it and it will Internally, deserialize and execute the callback.\n","x":-2760,"y":320,"width":1200,"height":1560},
		{"id":"f38901b60ae56321","x":-520,"y":840,"width":900,"height":1640,"type":"file","file":"Robo-Pope/Page API.md"}
	],
